A||||17||Pheagey||FOR THE LOVE OF FIEROS, HELP ME!!!!!||||9||
Z||000000||Pheagey||10-13-2001||07:51 PM||||Ok, there's the situation:<BR>   My '88 coupe was backfiring every time I would start my car, so as a starter I decided to change the plugs and wire (god knows when the other owner did it). So I get under the hood pull of the air filter and housing, spend an hour removing the plugs and wire and removing as much dirt and junk as possible. To the left of the engine block and just under the shifter cables is a cylindric looking mechanism the runs left to right almost directly above the axle. Since I was cleaning off dirt and all I moved the cylindric to the left and let it slowly push itself back out. I did this a few times as I removed dirt from the cylindric to ensure it was working as it should be.<BR>   So I installed the new plugs and wire, put the air filter & housing back on. I jump, push on the clutch (it felt a little 'loose', no force pushing back to me as it usually does; but I thought nothing of it). I turn the key and bingo! started without/ backfiring.<BR>   At this point I was a little pleased with/ my car and myself. But then I attempted to put it in gear- sh!t would not go into 1st. With the motor running and the clutch in it will not any gear; 1,2,3,4,5. On reverse it will sound as it would if you were rolling slowly and putting it in gear (the med/high pitched whining noise).<BR>   With the car off it will go into gear but at ignition the car leaches forward as if the clutch was not disengaged.<BR>   PLEASE PLEASE for the love of all that is good in fiero land I need to get this fixed. I'm an average mechanic on my car, oil, plugs, radio, dash work. I can not however drop the tranny for a rebuild or anything major like that; hopefully this will not require that as this car is my only transportation. If I don;t get this fixed by the end of tomorrow I'm in deep sh!t.<P><BR>PS= Sorry this was so long just wanted to make sure I got all the info here for a good diagnosis. (I am reading back posts in hopes of help also.)<p>[This message has been edited by Pheagey (edited 10-14-2001).]||||reg||9
